# An atom that names its own holder finds the holder at the enclosing level (plan M11 5a, the executor's reading B3):
# the atom is no record of A, so A\A is A itself, and so is A\A\A.
# Plan M11 5v: the declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call main().
# The path is read in the code of main (in_code) and from the root through main\data (seen); the enclosing level of A
# is now the data of main.
sub: main () (
    A:
        int: v 3
        A
    int: in_code 0
)
    in_code := A\A\A\v
main()
int: seen main\data\A\A\A\v
int: seen_in_code main\data\in_code
